ng surfaces cannot be manipulated in this manner for unknown reasons. Once an organism <em>feels</em> the affected area on the object (Rubbing against the object counts as feeling the object; Simply pressing against it does not), they spontaneously expire.</p> <p>There are several, non-kill agent anomalous properties to SCP-5645 that differ from the average <em>Homosapien</em>:</p> <ul> <li>SCP-5645 does not need to respirate.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>its organs continue to function even if outside of its body.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-5645 does not require sustinance in the form of food or drink. Despite this, it often requests to have food and beverages and has been observed eating and drinking.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-5645 does not expell waste products.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-5645 does not need to blink.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-5645 does not have blood.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-5645's wounds do not heal substantially slower than other non-anomalous <em>Homosapiens.</em><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-113403-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup></li> </ul> <ul> <li>Despite its wounds not healing, SCP-5645 does not respond to physical trauma.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-5645 claims to not feel pain.</li> </ul> <p>SCP-5645 was initially discovered in █████████, Spain after a spike in deaths occured, approximately double the average (1800 deaths a day). After a large group of the Cuerpo Nacional de Policía was sent to the center of the spike (█████████), SCP-5645 exited its house and emitted several auditory memetic kill agents. ██% of the group had expired before embedded agent ████ García notified the foundation. ███ more deaths occured before SCP-5645 was successfully contained and brought to Site-06-3.</p> <hr /> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Item&nbsp;Retrieval&nbsp;Log</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="displa